      "nets": ["unconnected-(U3-VBAT-Pad1)"],
      "observed": "The STM32L476RGT6 MCU (U3) has its VBAT pin (pin 1) left unconnected, with a no-connect flag in the netlist.",
      "expected": "Since the design has no backup battery (spec states no battery/regulator/USB part appears anywhere), the VBAT pin should be tied to the main VCC rail (VDD) per standard STM32 practice to power the backup domain.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"66\") (name \"unconnected-(U3-VBAT-Pad1)\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"VBAT\") (pintype \"power_in+no_connect\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "no battery, regulator, or USB part appears anywhere in the three .kicad_sch files or PCB.net/PCB.cir"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The MCU's backup domain (RTC, backup registers) may be unpowered or floating, potentially causing unreliable startup, increased current consumption, or failure of backup-domain functions.",
      "confidence": 0.8
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain one anomaly: the STM32 MCU's VBAT pin is left unconnected despite the absence of a backup battery, which deviates from standard practice and the intended design."
}

